# Write-once transcript vault: local recovery copies of completed 8x8 transcripts.
# Regenerable from hardware/s8_*/transcript; ~0.4 GB and not review material.
docs/benchmarks/8x8_scaleup/transcript_vault/

# Per-shape apps emitted by scripts/gen_decode_shape_app.sh. Generated from the matmul source
# plus MATMUL_DECODE_SPLIT; the ELF is copied to hardware/ and is standalone, so the app dir is
# a build artifact. Committing generated shape apps is what left 1064 sp-fp16-* files in the
# tree; do not repeat it for decode.
# Per-shape decode app dirs were GENERATED, one per shape, and drifted into 5 distinct
# main.c versions before being merged. Only shape-named dirs are generated now.
software/apps/spatz_apps/sp-decode-[0-9]*/
# sp-decode-fp16 / sp-decode-fp32 ARE source (main.c and kernel are symlinks to the
# canonical sp-fmatmul-opt-burst-merge{,-fp16}), but their shape spec and the 16-36 MB
# data header are generated at build time from gemm_m/gemm_n/gemm_p.
# The canonical apps carry BOTH regimes now (main.c auto-derives MATMUL_DECODE_SPLIT), so
# their shape spec and 16-36 MB data header are generated per build from gemm_m/n/p.
software/apps/spatz_apps/sp-fmatmul-opt-burst-merge/script/matmul.json
software/apps/spatz_apps/sp-fmatmul-opt-burst-merge/data/data_gemm.h
software/apps/spatz_apps/sp-fmatmul-opt-burst-merge-fp16/script/matmul.json
software/apps/spatz_apps/sp-fmatmul-opt-burst-merge-fp16/data/data_gemm.h
